(4, 'blog', 1, 2, 5, NULL, 'The Government Has Slashed Out The Stamp Duty', 'the-government-has-slashed-out-the-stamp-duty', NULL, 'The chairman of the Real Estate & Housing Association of Bangladesh Mr. Liakat Ali Bhuiyan expressed their satisfaction regarding stamp duty reduction', '<p><strong>The government has decreased the stamp duty on transferring land and flats from 3 percent to 1.5 percent on property registration.</strong></p>\r\n<p>On December 24th the finance ministry&rsquo;s Internal Resources Division has issued a gazette notification with the sign of Md Mosharraf Hossain Bhuiyan senior secretary IRD as well as chairman of the National Board of Revenue (NRB).</p>\r\n<p><em>The chairman of the Real Estate &amp; Housing Association of Bangladesh Mr. Liakat Ali Bhuiyan expressed their satisfaction regarding stamp duty reduction. He also asked for a reduction in the registration fee, local govt. tax and land development vat to live up people&rsquo;s hope. Also, the finance ministry, as well as the revenue board, requested the ministry and the division to take required steps to reduce fees from 2 percent to 1 percent from 2 percent to 1.5 percent for the local government tax.</em></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><em><img src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"\" width=\"977\" height=\"490\"></em></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 18pt;\">REHAB has informed that currently, buyers are paying 4 percent gain tax, 2 percent registration fee, 2 percent local govt. Tax and 3 percent of land development vat ( total 7 percent ) for flat registration. Due to this, a large number of properties remain unsold.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p>One of the REHAB members also said that the execution of the decision of decreasing stamp duty along with other fees-taxes would put an effective impact on the real estate sector. The rate of flats and plots sales, as well as registration, would increase.</p>', '<p>The government has decreased the stamp duty on transferring land and flats from 3 percent to 1.5 percent on property registration.</p>\r\n<p>On December 24th the finance ministry&rsquo;s Internal Resources Division has issued a gazette notification with the sign of Md Mosharraf Hossain Bhuiyan senior secretary IRD as well as chairman of the National Board of Revenue (NRB).</p>\r\n<p>The chairman of the Real Estate &amp; Housing Association of Bangladesh Mr. Liakat Ali Bhuiyan expressed their satisfaction regarding stamp duty reduction. He also asked for a reduction in the registration fee, local govt. tax and land development vat to live up people&rsquo;s hope. Also, the finance ministry, as well as the revenue board, requested the ministry and the division to take required steps to reduce fees from 2 percent to 1 percent from 2 percent to 1.5 percent for the local government tax.</p>\r\n<p>REHAB has informed that currently, buyers are paying 4 percent gain tax, 2 percent registration fee, 2 percent local govt. Tax and 3 percent of land development vat ( total 7 percent ) for flat registration. Due to this, a large number of properties remain unsold.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>One of the REHAB members also said that the execution of the decision of decreasing stamp duty along with other fees-taxes would put an effective impact on the real estate sector. The rate of flats and plots sales, as well as registration, would increase.</p>', NULL, NULL, '[]', '[]', NULL, NULL, 'uploads/blog/img_6a339d7613a92_1781767542.webp', '[\"uploads/blog/img_6a339d76891ba_1781767542.webp\", \"uploads/blog/img_6a339d76895df_1781767542.webp\"]', 'uploads/project/videos/853X6hrJ1MFFdzhIOxWgwJXTltWAJrVYMyDmn1zS.mp4', NULL, '[]', '2026-06-25 17:15:00', NULL, 'The Government Has Slashed Out The Stamp Duty', 'The chairman of the Real Estate & Housing Association of Bangladesh Mr. Liakat Ali Bhuiyan expressed their satisfaction regarding stamp duty reduction', 'housing housing-abason,stamp duty', 1, 79, 1, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-06-18 01:25:42', '2026-08-17 05:33:29'),
